# WAIA design canon (implementation)

## Source documents

- **Creative + systemic language:** `docs/DESIGN_OS_V1.md`
- **Production tokens + Tailwind bridge:** `docs/DESIGN_FOUNDATION_V1.md`
- **Canonical CSS variables:** `app/design/tokens-waia.css`
- **Tailwind `@theme` + dark shadcn bridge:** `app/globals.css`

## Engineering rules

1. **Prefer WAIA semantics** in new UI: Tailwind `waia-*` colors (`bg-waia-field`, `text-waia-fg-muted`, `text-waia-accent-warm`, etc.), `spacing-waia-*`, `radius-waia-*`, `blur-waia-*`, `shadow-waia-glow-warm`, durations/easings `duration-waia-base`, `ease-waia-settle`. Use `bg-primary` / `text-foreground` only when inheriting shadcn components; in `.dark` these map to WAIA via the bridge.
2. **No raw hex** for brand surfaces; use `var(--waia-…)` or Tailwind token classes. Instrumental colors (`waia-danger`, etc.) are allowed exceptions only through tokens.
3. **Atmosphere** (`--waia-atmo-*` gradients, heavy blur, glow stacks): **ceremonial surfaces only** (auth, onboarding, rare milestones)—not the default dashboard/chat chrome.
4. **Accent budget:** one dominant warm glow focal per viewport; avoid competing halos.
5. **`prefers-reduced-motion`:** implement calm degradations when adding motion; see Design OS motion tiering.
6. Do not drift toward cyberpunk/neon, crypto gold, gaming HUD, or gratuitous glass stacks—Design OS §14.
7. **Copy / register anti-drift:** Design vocabulary in product copy, marketing pages, partner decks, and onboarding text must avoid techno-spiritual, luxury-mystic, or cultic register. Re-anchor on [`WAIA-NORTH-STAR.md`](../../docs/waia-governance/WAIA-NORTH-STAR.md) §3 (human-centered constraints) and §6 (anti-drift guardrails), not Design OS §1–§2 elevated vocabulary alone.

## Typography

- UI body: default `font-sans` (existing stack).
- Brand / reflective moments: `font-waia-serif` + size via `text-[length:var(--waia-type-display)]` or inline `style` for line-height from tokens where utilities are not yet wired.
